  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure will continue to dominate through the early part \nof next week. A weakening cold front will drop south across the\narea this afternoon into the evening, with the front only\nproducing increased clouds. This should allow for slightly \ncooler temperatures Friday followed by a warming trend this \nweekend. A tightening pressure gradient between the frontal\npassage, high pressure to the northwest and a storm off the\nAtlantic coast will cause an increase in winds this afternoon\nwith gusts to 20 mph possible at times. The other issue to take\ninto account is a typical model high bias of afternoon \ndewpoints in this pattern, RGEM model not as biased here, so\nblended that in through Sunday. \n\nYet another cold front attempts to break down the ridge a bit \nearly next week but also looks moisture starved. The pattern overall \nthrough most of next week remains dry or with brief passing showers \nlater in the week.",
